{"id": "f42e2279-1e15-4e2b-b4ec-a4cc95fbb831", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T13:42:43.112107", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "82236d33-c4c8-4c01-8810-029fd35e05e2", "action": {"command": "cat > /workspace/final_design.md <<'EOF'\n# Final Design — Credibility of Docta-Cleaned Labels via Predictive Performance, Validated by ChatGPT and In-House Human Annotators on Their Disagreements\n\n**Stage:** design-only (submission). No experiments executed. No network access. No external dependencies.\n**Evidence base:** `/workspace/task.json` alone. `/workspace/track.md` is absent on disk (its `documents.track.md` value is a meta-note string, not a file). `researcher_topics` is `[]`. No Docta paper, dataset, code, or ChatGPT endpoint is bundled.\n**Approved approach (locked):** D1–D8 defaults verbatim; Q1 = R-S (ChatGPT as frozen independent label stream `y_gpt`); Q2 = whole-evaluation PLUS conditional as a co-requirement, with whole-eval sign acting as a *gate* on the conditional credibility claim; Q3 = R-T three-way fold (`y_gpt`, `y_human`, `y_adjudicator`) on `D_dis`, senior adjudicator is a **NEW role** distinct from D6 line annotators; Q4 = OP-A (single offline-generated noisy-label classification task with declared noise injection), OP-B noise-rate sweep (`p ∈ {0.10, 0.30, 0.50}`) staged as out-of-scope extension; Docta treatment = **D-mock** with a *committed* specific transformation (below), frozen now.\n\n---\n\n## (i) Executive summary — answer to the brief, with a falsifiable decision rule\n\n**Hypothesis (this design lets the runtime stage either confirm or refute):** *The labels cleaned by Docta demonstrate higher credibility than the raw labels, reflected in (a) better downstream classifier predictive performance on the full held-out test set, AND (b) better downstream classifier predictive performance specifically on the disagreement slice `D_dis = { i : y_gpt[i] ≠ y_human[i] }`, where the comparison is jointly validated by ChatGPT and in-house human annotators and resolved by a blind senior adjudicator on contested items.*\n\n**Falsifiable decision rule (pre-registered; all four conditions must hold at the run-time stage for a \"YES\" verdict; otherwise the brief's question receives a \"NO\" verdict with a diagnostic label on which gate failed):**\n\n1. **Whole-evaluation gate (Q2 co-requirement):** `macroF1(M_clean, D_test) − macroF1(M_raw, D_test) ≥ δ_te`, with `δ_te = 0.03` (binary) or `δ_te = 0.05` (k > 2), under paired bootstrap 95% CI whose lower bound may be negative *only* by at most `−δ_te/2` and only if the point estimate is positive. A negative point estimate, or a CI entirely below zero, FAILS the gate regardless of conditional evidence.\n2. **Conditional test:** On `D_dis`, paired permutation test (k > 2) or exact McNemar (binary) on the same metric yields a two-sided `p ≤ α_family / m` under Holm-Bonferroni with `α_family = 0.05` and `m = 4` family sub-tests (whole-eval, D_dis primary, D_dis replication slice, D_dis adjudicator-vs-both sensitivity corner case — the last reported, not primary). The macro-F1 paired bootstrap 95% CI on `D_dis` excludes zero.\n3. **Power precondition (D5):** `|D_dis| ≥ 50` usable items with non-empty overlap in both `y_raw` and `y_clean` label streams for the same items.\n4. **Leakage constraint (D8):** `D_gold ∩ (D_raw-train ∪ D_clean-train) = ∅` and `D_gold ∩ D_test = ∅`.\n\n**Verdict mapping:**\n- All four ⇒ **\"DOCTA-CLEANED LABELS DEMONSTRATE HIGHER CREDIBILITY UNDER THE BRIEF\"** (YES, with three sub-verdicts reported: full test, `D_dis` primary, `D_dis` replication slice all PSS — pre-registered sign-success).\n- Gate 1 fails ⇒ **NO, diagnostic = `WHOLE-EVAL-DID-NOT-CREDIT`** (conditional results reported but explicitly downgraded and not counted as a credibility win).\n- Gate 2 fails ⇒ **NO, diagnostic = `CONDITIONAL-DID-NOT-CREDIT`**.\n- Gate 3 fails ⇒ **INCONCLUSIVE — INSUFFICIENT `D_dis` POWER**, no claim made; runtime stage must rerun with resampling or adjust eligibility.\n- Gate 4 fails ⇒ **DESIGN VIOLATION**, runtime stage aborts and fixes splits.\n\nThis decision rule is the falsifiable hook the brief requires.\n\n---\n\n## (ii) Rationale — how the design links to A/B/C and to the locked defaults\n\nThe three-check outline from the planning round carries over directly:\n\n- **(A) Predictive comparison (check A) → primary metric layer.** Tightened by D2/D3/D4/D8 to \"paired macro-F1 with bootstrap CIs and pre-registered McNemar (binary) / paired permutation (k > 2) on a `D_test` held out from both training streams and from `D_gold`.\" This becomes the **gate (gate 1)** under Q2's whole-evaluation co-requirement.\n- **(B) ChatGPT's role (check B) → frozen label-stream indexer of `D_dis` under R-S (Q1).** Per Q1, ChatGPT is not asked to issue raw-vs-clean pass/fail verdicts on predictions; it is run once under a frozen snapshot and frozen prompt to produce `y_gpt[i]`, and `D_dis = { i : y_gpt[i] ≠ y_human[i] }` is the disagreement-indexing machinery. ChatGPT's downstream judgement on `M_raw` vs `M_clean` predictions is reported only as a secondary descriptor of agreement with humans (Cohen's κ on the agreement slice; reported but not the credibility verdict).\n- **(C) Human authority (check C) → three-way fold under R-T (Q3).** On each `D_dis` item, the headline label is the result of a deterministic function of `y_gpt`, `y_human` (built from ≥ 2 D6 line annotators with senior adjudicator tie-break — D6), and a fresh independent `y_adj` from the senior adjudicator NEW role, blind to raw/clean provenance and to the ChatGPT snapshot. The headline resolution is the adjudicator's label; cases where the adjudicator disagrees with both validators are kept as a **sensitivity slice (control SL-2 below)** but do not override the headline.\n\nDefaults D1 (no live execution), D5 (≥ 50 conditional items), D6 (≥ 2 line annotators, blind tie-break via D6 senior adjudicator), D7 (frozen snapshot + frozen prompt + open-LLM substitute disclosure) are enforced as written. D-mock Docta is concrete (section iii).\n\nEOF\necho \"chunk1 OK\"; wc -c /workspace/final_design.md", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-3d302a4e-0b8d-4a20-9073-fe665e6000bc", "tool_call": {"id": "call-3d302a4e-0b8d-4a20-9073-fe665e6000bc", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Write final_design.md chunk 1\", \"command\": \"cat > /workspace/final_design.md <<'EOF'\\n# Final Design \\u2014 Credibility of Docta-Cleaned Labels via Predictive Performance, Validated by ChatGPT and In-House Human Annotators on Their Disagreements\\n\\n**Stage:** design-only (submission). No experiments executed. No network access. No external dependencies.\\n**Evidence base:** `/workspace/task.json` alone. `/workspace/track.md` is absent on disk (its `documents.track.md` value is a meta-note string, not a file). `researcher_topics` is `[]`. No Docta paper, dataset, code, or ChatGPT endpoint is bundled.\\n**Approved approach (locked):** D1\\u2013D8 defaults verbatim; Q1 = R-S (ChatGPT as frozen independent label stream `y_gpt`); Q2 = whole-evaluation PLUS conditional as a co-requirement, with whole-eval sign acting as a *gate* on the conditional credibility claim; Q3 = R-T three-way fold (`y_gpt`, `y_human`, `y_adjudicator`) on `D_dis`, senior adjudicator is a **NEW role** distinct from D6 line annotators; Q4 = OP-A (single offline-generated noisy-label classification task with declared noise injection), OP-B noise-rate sweep (`p \\u2208 {0.10, 0.30, 0.50}`) staged as out-of-scope extension; Docta treatment = **D-mock** with a *committed* specific transformation (below), frozen now.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (i) Executive summary \\u2014 answer to the brief, with a falsifiable decision rule\\n\\n**Hypothesis (this design lets the runtime stage either confirm or refute):** *The labels cleaned by Docta demonstrate higher credibility than the raw labels, reflected in (a) better downstream classifier predictive performance on the full held-out test set, AND (b) better downstream classifier predictive performance specifically on the disagreement slice `D_dis = { i : y_gpt[i] \\u2260 y_human[i] }`, where the comparison is jointly validated by ChatGPT and in-house human annotators and resolved by a blind senior adjudicator on contested items.*\\n\\n**Falsifiable decision rule (pre-registered; all four conditions must hold at the run-time stage for a \\\"YES\\\" verdict; otherwise the brief's question receives a \\\"NO\\\" verdict with a diagnostic label on which gate failed):**\\n\\n1. **Whole-evaluation gate (Q2 co-requirement):** `macroF1(M_clean, D_test) \\u2212 macroF1(M_raw, D_test) \\u2265 \\u03b4_te`, with `\\u03b4_te = 0.03` (binary) or `\\u03b4_te = 0.05` (k > 2), under paired bootstrap 95% CI whose lower bound may be negative *only* by at most `\\u2212\\u03b4_te/2` and only if the point estimate is positive. A negative point estimate, or a CI entirely below zero, FAILS the gate regardless of conditional evidence.\\n2. **Conditional test:** On `D_dis`, paired permutation test (k > 2) or exact McNemar (binary) on the same metric yields a two-sided `p \\u2264 \\u03b1_family / m` under Holm-Bonferroni with `\\u03b1_family = 0.05` and `m = 4` family sub-tests (whole-eval, D_dis primary, D_dis replication slice, D_dis adjudicator-vs-both sensitivity corner case \\u2014 the last reported, not primary). The macro-F1 paired bootstrap 95% CI on `D_dis` excludes zero.\\n3. **Power precondition (D5):** `|D_dis| \\u2265 50` usable items with non-empty overlap in both `y_raw` and `y_clean` label streams for the same items.\\n4. **Leakage constraint (D8):** `D_gold \\u2229 (D_raw-train \\u222a D_clean-train) = \\u2205` and `D_gold \\u2229 D_test = \\u2205`.\\n\\n**Verdict mapping:**\\n- All four \\u21d2 **\\\"DOCTA-CLEANED LABELS DEMONSTRATE HIGHER CREDIBILITY UNDER THE BRIEF\\\"** (YES, with three sub-verdicts reported: full test, `D_dis` primary, `D_dis` replication slice all PSS \\u2014 pre-registered sign-success).\\n- Gate 1 fails \\u21d2 **NO, diagnostic = `WHOLE-EVAL-DID-NOT-CREDIT`** (conditional results reported but explicitly downgraded and not counted as a credibility win).\\n- Gate 2 fails \\u21d2 **NO, diagnostic = `CONDITIONAL-DID-NOT-CREDIT`**.\\n- Gate 3 fails \\u21d2 **INCONCLUSIVE \\u2014 INSUFFICIENT `D_dis` POWER**, no claim made; runtime stage must rerun with resampling or adjust eligibility.\\n- Gate 4 fails \\u21d2 **DESIGN VIOLATION**, runtime stage aborts and fixes splits.\\n\\nThis decision rule is the falsifiable hook the brief requires.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (ii) Rationale \\u2014 how the design links to A/B/C and to the locked defaults\\n\\nThe three-check outline from the planning round carries over directly:\\n\\n- **(A) Predictive comparison (check A) \\u2192 primary metric layer.** Tightened by D2/D3/D4/D8 to \\\"paired macro-F1 with bootstrap CIs and pre-registered McNemar (binary) / paired permutation (k > 2) on a `D_test` held out from both training streams and from `D_gold`.\\\" This becomes the **gate (gate 1)** under Q2's whole-evaluation co-requirement.\\n- **(B) ChatGPT's role (check B) \\u2192 frozen label-stream indexer of `D_dis` under R-S (Q1).** Per Q1, ChatGPT is not asked to issue raw-vs-clean pass/fail verdicts on predictions; it is run once under a frozen snapshot and frozen prompt to produce `y_gpt[i]`, and `D_dis = { i : y_gpt[i] \\u2260 y_human[i] }` is the disagreement-indexing machinery. ChatGPT's downstream judgement on `M_raw` vs `M_clean` predictions is reported only as a secondary descriptor of agreement with humans (Cohen's \\u03ba on the agreement slice; reported but not the credibility verdict).\\n- **(C) Human authority (check C) \\u2192 three-way fold under R-T (Q3).** On each `D_dis` item, the headline label is the result of a deterministic function of `y_gpt`, `y_human` (built from \\u2265 2 D6 line annotators with senior adjudicator tie-break \\u2014 D6), and a fresh independent `y_adj` from the senior adjudicator NEW role, blind to raw/clean provenance and to the ChatGPT snapshot. The headline resolution is the adjudicator's label; cases where the adjudicator disagrees with both validators are kept as a **sensitivity slice (control SL-2 below)** but do not override the headline.\\n\\nDefaults D1 (no live execution), D5 (\\u2265 50 conditional items), D6 (\\u2265 2 line annotators, blind tie-break via D6 senior adjudicator), D7 (frozen snapshot + frozen prompt + open-LLM substitute disclosure) are enforced as written. D-mock Docta is concrete (section iii).\\n\\nEOF\\necho \\\"chunk1 OK\\\"; wc -c /workspace/final_design.md\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-1ae720d0-c06d-4b56-8f29-c37b5c8d4134", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 28}
