{"id": "e521cc22-24a9-4ee5-86db-3b26299a9dbc", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T13:43:56.680447", "source": "environment", "parent_id": "7dd48e99-97ba-4633-a228-562f380ab61f", "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-753d39b1-506b-4e20-8e30-efb6cd70dbb6", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"phase\": \"exploration\", \"command\": \"cat >> /workspace/final_design.md <<'EOF'\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (iii) End-to-end experimental design\\n\\n### iii.1 Dataset binding (OP-A primary, OP-B out-of-scope extension)\\n\\n**OP-A (committed primary):** A single offline-generated noisy-label classification task synthesised in this workspace at runtime under the following declarations. No external download, no network, pure-Python 3.12.3.\\n\\n- **Base distribution:** Gaussian mixture with declared `(k, d, n_per_class)` fixed at runtime stage. Per-class means `\\u03bc_c` are sampled i.i.d. from `N(0, I_d)` once with a frozen seed; covariance = `\\u03c3\\u00b2 I_d` with `\\u03c3 = 1.0` (runtime-fillable, frozen before split).\\n- **Number of classes `k`:** committed to `k = 5` for primary analysis (forces usage of the paired permutation test rather than defaulting to McNemar; exercises the k > 2 branch of D4).\\n- **Sample size `N`:** committed range `6,000 \\u2264 N \\u2264 10,000`, with `N = N_test + N_train + N_gold` (split sizes below).\\n- **True labels:** assigned by component.\\n- **Noise injection (declared):** class-conditional symmetric label noise with rate `p = 0.30` as primary, applied to the *raw* label stream `y_raw` only. Symmetric means `Q_raw[y_obs, y_true] = (1 \\u2212 p)` if `y_obs = y_true`, else `p / (k \\u2212 1)`. The frozen seed for noise injection is logged.\\n- **Auxiliary `aux_noise`:** the noise model itself persisted in the run log so the design-level audit can verify injection was applied as declared.\\n- **Features, prompts, identifiers:** all random generation via `random.Random(seed)` with a single document-level seed persisted in the run log.\\n\\n**OP-B (out-of-scope; documented extension if reviewer requests curve evidence):** rerun the entire pipeline at `p \\u2208 {0.10, 0.30, 0.50}` using the same frozen seeds and same `D_test` indices. Used for stability evidence (control SL-4); *not* required for the headline verdict.\\n\\n### iii.2 Split discipline (train / raw-train / clean-train / D_gold / D_test)\\n\\nFive disjoint item-index sets, all on `D_synth`:\\n\\n```\\nD_synth\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 D_train        \\u2500\\u2500 features only; shared backbone\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 D_raw_train  \\u2500\\u2500 noisy raw labels (OP-A noise applied)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 D_clean_train \\u2500\\u2500 Docta D-mock cleaned labels (transformation below)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 D_gold         \\u2500\\u2500 features + line-annotator + adjudicator labels\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 D_test         \\u2500\\u2500 features only; raw-only eval labels y_raw_test (used for M_raw)\\n```\\n\\n- **Sizes (committed ranges):** `|D_train| \\u2248 0.7 N`, `|D_gold| \\u2248 0.15 N`, `|D_test| \\u2248 0.15 N`, with absolute minimums `|D_train| \\u2265 4,000`, `|D_gold| \\u2265 900`, `|D_test| \\u2265 900`.\\n- **Disjointness (D8):** `D_train \\u2229 D_gold = \\u2205`, `D_train \\u2229 D_test = \\u2205`, `D_gold \\u2229 D_test = \\u2205`. Both `D_raw_train` and `D_clean_train` are subsets of `D_train`, so disjointness against `D_gold` and `D_test` holds automatically.\\n- **Seeding:** split determined by a deterministic hash of the document-level seed; exact indices written to the run log and reused across `M_raw`, `M_clean`, and the null comparison used in control SL-3.\\n\\n### iii.3 Docta D-mock transformation (committed; frozen now)\\n\\nA specific, seeded, probabilistic, confusion-matrix-aware label-denoising transformation. **Not** the abstract class.\\n\\n**Inputs (committed):**\\n- Training stream with raw labels `y_raw` on items in `D_train`.\\n- Declared noise matrix `Q_raw` (symmetric, OP-A injection at `p = 0.30`, k = 5): `Q[ty, ky] = P(noisy = ty | true = ky)`.\\n- Document-level seed `s`.\\n\\n**Algorithm (frozen):**\\n\\n1. **Backbone training (one-time):** fit an `L2`-regularised multinomial logistic regression `h` on `(x_i, y_raw[i])` for `i \\u2208 D_train`, with regularisation strength `\\u03bb` selected by 5-fold cross-validated held-out macro-F1 within `D_train`. Implementation: pure-Python fixed-step gradient descent, step `\\u03b7 = 1e-3`, `max_iter = 200`, `min_iter = 25`, convergence threshold `|L(\\u03b8_t) \\u2212 L(\\u03b8_{t\\u22121})| < 1e-5`. Per-class learning-rate scaling `\\u03b7_c = \\u03b7 / max(1, n_train_c / (N_train / k))`. Frozen seed `s` controls fold partitioning and stochastic tie-breaks. The resulting `h(x; \\u03b8)` is stored as a function and not retrained. (Runtime-fillable grid: `\\u03bb \\u2208 {1e-4, 1e-3, 1e-2, 1e-1}`, frozen once selected.)\\n2. **Iterative noise-matrix re-estimation (bounded EM):**\\n   - Initialise `Q_t \\u2190 Q_raw`.\\n   - For `t \\u2208 {1, 2, 3}`:\\n     - Compute posterior `P(true = ky | x_i, y_raw[i]) \\u221d Q_t[y_raw[i], ky] \\u00b7 h(x_i; \\u03b8)[ky]`, renormalised.\\n     - `Q_new[ty, ky] = ( \\u03a3_i 1{y_raw[i] = ty} \\u00b7 P(true = ky | x_i, y_raw[i]) + \\u03b5 ) / ( \\u03a3_i P(true = ky | x_i, y_raw[i]) + k\\u03b5 )`, `\\u03b5 = 1e-3`.\\n     - `Q_t \\u2190 0.5 \\u00b7 Q_new + 0.5 \\u00b7 Q_t`.\\n     - If `\\u2016Q_t \\u2212 Q_{t\\u22121}\\u2016_\\u221e < 1e-3` break.\\n   - Output final `Q*` and per-item posterior.\\n3. **Final posterior and cleaned labels:** On each `i \\u2208 D_train`, `P*(true = ky | x_i, y_raw[i]) \\u221d Q*[y_raw[i], ky] \\u00b7 h(x_i; \\u03b8)[ky]`, renormalised. Set `y_clean[i] = argmax_ky P*(true = ky | x_i, y_raw[i])`, deterministic tie-break: smallest class index.\\n4. **Output:** function mapping each `i \\u2208 D_train` to `y_clean[i]` plus per-item posterior table.\\n\\n**Properties guaranteed by this commitment:**\\n- **Seed-deterministic:** identical inputs + identical `s` \\u21d2 identical `y_clean`.\\n- **Confusion-matrix-aware:** cleaning explicitly conditions on per-class confusion structure.\\n- **Probabilistic at each step:** posterior is genuinely Bayesian (point estimate under frozen estimator).\\n- **Pure-Python implementable** for committed bounds `d \\u2264 100`, `k = 5`.\\n- **Bounded compute:** EM capped at 3 iterations; in practice converges in 2 under the OP-A noise model.\\n\\nLogged in run record as `docta_mock_v1.confusion_matrix_aware.bounded_em.k5_lambda_freeze`. The *only* D-mock used; no swap at runtime.\\n\\n### iii.4 ChatGPT invocation (D7)\\n\\n- **Default model:** `gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18` (frozen snapshot), `temperature = 0`, `top_p = 1`, `seed` = run's document-level seed.\\n- **Frozen prompt template:**\\n  ```\\n  System: You are an expert annotator assigned to label items in {task_name}.\\n  The label space is exactly: {labels_csv}.\\n  Reply with EXACTLY one label string and nothing else.\\n\\n  User:\\n  Item id: {item_id}\\n  Features (JSON, double-quoted): {x_json}\\n  Auxiliary context: none.\\n\\n  Label:\\n  ```\\n  No in-context examples, no reasoning trace, no chain-of-thought \\u2014 frozen to keep prompt-induced variance at zero.\\n- **Per-item retry policy:** if response is not parseable into one of the declared labels, retry once with `temperature = 0` and an appended reminder. If still unparseable, label = `UNCERTAIN`; excluded from `y_gpt` and from `D_dis` indexing. Report the unparseable rate as a quality descriptor.\\n- **D-mock surrogate fallback (D7 substitute):** if no ChatGPT endpoint is reachable, swap to a deterministic seeded surrogate from the same backbone `h(x; \\u03b8)` with `temperature = 0` and label = `argmax h(x; \\u03b8)`. Disclose substitution in the header of every results table. Verdict interpreted identically.\\n- **What ChatGPT is *not* asked to do:** never asked to score or rank predictions of `M_raw` vs `M_clean`; never shown raw or clean labels; never shown `y_human` or `y_adjudicator`.\\n\\n### iii.5 Human annotation pipeline (D6 + Q3 NEW role)\\n\\n- **Line annotators (D6):** \\u2265 2 independent in-house human annotators per `D_gold` item. Annotators blind to raw/clean/ChatGPT labels and to model predictions. Each provides one of the committed k = 5 labels plus a binary confidence flag (high / low). Hashed annotator IDs persisted.\\n- **`y_human` construction (committed deterministic rule):**\\n  - Both annotators agree, both high-confidence \\u21d2 `y_human[i]` = agreed label.\\n  - Annotators disagree \\u21d2 senior adjudicator (NEW role, Q3) consulted *once* for `y_human[i]`, blind to the specific labels annotators provided; one-line justification recorded for audit. Consumes adjudicator-hours at the rate of `|disagreements inside D_gold|`.\\n  - Both agree but \\u2265 1 low-confidence \\u21d2 `REQUIRES_REVIEW`; excluded from `D_dis` indexing; reported but not used in headline tests.\\n- **Senior adjudicator (NEW role, Q3) \\u2014 two distinct invocations:**\\n  - *Invocation A (D6 tie-break):* above, for `y_human` construction.\\n  - *Invocation B (D_dis analysis fold):* for each `i \\u2208 D_dis`, adjudicator emits an independent `y_adj[i]` from the same item feature representation, blind to `y_human[i]`, `y_gpt[i]`, raw/clean provenance, and `M_raw` / `M_clean` predictions. `y_adj[i]` is the **headline label** on `D_dis` for the primary metric.\\n- **Blinding log:** every adjudication call records a JSON line of items seen, formatted prompt, returned label, time-on-task.\\n\\n### iii.6 Disagreement-indexing rule (Q1 + Q2)\\n\\n`y_gpt[i]` (iii.4) and `y_human[i]` (iii.5) produced for all `i \\u2208 D_gold`. `D_dis = { i \\u2208 D_gold : y_gpt[i] \\u2260 y_human[i] \\u2227 y_human[i] \\u2260 REQUIRES_REVIEW }`. Symmetric exclusion: items where `y_gpt[i] = UNCERTAIN` also excluded.\\n\\n`D_dis` computed **once, before** any analysis-step invocation on `M_raw` or `M_clean` predictions, and frozen. Sensitivity to threshold-only changes (e.g., top-decile labelling-confidence disagreement instead of exact disagreement) reported as a control. `D_dis` is the sub-population for the conditional test; whole-evaluation test uses the full `D_test`. Q2's gate (gate 1) is the whole-evaluation test.\\n\\nEOF\\necho \\\"chunk2 OK\\\"; wc -c /workspace/final_design.md\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.068, \"output\": \"chunk2 OK\\n15139 /workspace/final_design.md\\n\", \"output_truncated\": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "7dd48e99-97ba-4633-a228-562f380ab61f", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent", "source_event_index": 33}
{"id": "f5305ca5-95d8-4428-96de-a653da76e01f", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T13:44:04.618481", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "e521cc22-24a9-4ee5-86db-3b26299a9dbc", "action": {"command": "cat >> /workspace/final_design.md <<'EOF'\n\n---\n\n## (iv) Controls (minimum required)\n\nEach control is registered, named, and given a role in the analysis plan. Reported in a fixed order.\n\n1. **SL-1 — Untouched `D_dis` replication slice.** Within `D_dis`, before any adjudication call, randomly withhold 30% of `D_dis` items as a *replication set* `D_dis_repl`. The remaining 70% (`D_dis_train_of_test`) is used for the primary conditional test; `D_dis_repl` is evaluated exactly once at the end using the same frozen `y_adj`, frozen `M_raw`, frozen `M_clean` predictions. A positive primary result that fails to reproduce in `D_dis_repl` (same sign) downgrades the verdict from \"YES\" to \"INCONCLUSIVE — REPLICATION FAILED\".\n2. **SL-2 — Adjudicator-vs-both sensitivity slice.** Items on which `y_adj[i]` disagrees with **both** `y_gpt[i]` and `y_human[i]`. Reported as a descriptor; **not in the primary metric family** and **not in the FWER family**. Used to characterise the irreducible noise floor of single-adjudicator resolutions when both validators diverge.\n3. **SL-3 — Label-shuffled null.** Construct a third label stream `y_shuf` by permuting `y_raw` uniformly at random within each class (preserves marginal class distribution; destroys conditioned-on-feature signal). Train a third model `M_shuf` identically to `M_raw` (same backbone, same hyper-parameters, same splits). Expect `macroF1(M_shuf, D_test) ≈ 1/k = 0.20` for k = 5. If macro-F1 on `M_shuf` exceeds macro-F1 on `M_clean`, treat as **DESIGN VIOLATION** regardless of other gates. Reports point estimate and 95% bootstrap CI; **in the primary metric family for FWER**.\n4. **SL-4 — Noise-rate sweep from OP-B (stability evidence, out of runtime scope by default).** Re-run the entire pipeline at `p ∈ {0.10, 0.30, 0.50}` keeping s