{"id": "ac786de3-0c91-4c66-bd63-96165c55c2fb", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T13:44:19.165355", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "22ed0913-f19a-4a7a-85c3-0d02088c94db", "action": {"command": "cat >> /workspace/final_design.md <<'EOF'\n\n---\n\n## (v) Pre-registered analysis plan\n\n### v.1 Metrics\n\n- **Primary:** macro-F1 (unweighted mean of per-class F1 over `k = 5` classes).\n- **Secondary:** accuracy, error rate (`1 − accuracy`).\n- **Agreement / quality descriptors:** Cohen's κ between `y_gpt` and `y_human` on `D_gold \\ REQUIRES_REVIEW`; UNCERTAIN rate; adjudicator-vs-both disagreement rate; per-annotator inter-annotator agreement.\n\n### v.2 Statistical tests (D3, D4)\n\n- **Whole-evaluation gate (gate 1):**\n  - Paired macro-F1 difference `Δ_full = macroF1(M_clean, D_test) − macroF1(M_raw, D_test)` with paired bootstrap 95% CI, `B = 2,000` resamples.\n  - Pre-registered effect-size threshold `δ_te = 0.05` for k = 5 (binary `δ_te = 0.03` if k = 2 in any branch).\n  - Two-sided paired permutation test on per-item class-correctness indicators, `M = 10,000` permutations, with the same `m = 4` family Holm-Bonferroni structure (gate 1 = member 1, gate 2 primary = member 2, SL-1 replication = member 3, SL-3 null = member 4; SL-2 not in FWER family).\n- **Conditional test (gate 2 primary):**\n  - Computed on `D_dis_train_of_test` (post SL-1 withholding).\n  - Paired permutation test `M = 10,000`, two-sided, on macro-F1 contribution at the class level.\n  - Paired bootstrap 95% CI on macro-F1 difference `Δ_dis`.\n  - For a binary-schema path (only invoked if committed `k = 5` is overridden at runtime): exact McNemar on the discordant indicator `1{y_pred_raw == y_adj} ⊕ 1{y_pred_clean == y_adj}`.\n\n### v.3 Decision rule (full, consolidated)\n\n| Gate | Test | Threshold | FWER family member |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Whole-eval paired permutation on `D_test`; CI excludes 0; `Δ_full ≥ δ_te` | `p_adj ≤ α_family / 4` | 1 |\n| 2 | Conditional paired permutation on `D_dis_train_of_test`; CI excludes 0; `Δ_dis ≥ δ_co` | `p_adj ≤ α_family / 4`, `δ_co = 0.05` | 2 |\n| 3 | SL-1 replication on `D_dis_repl`; CI excludes 0; same sign | `p_adj ≤ α_family / 4` | 3 |\n| 4 | SL-3 null — `macroF1(M_shuf) ≤ 1/k + 1e-2` | point estimate bound | 4 |\n\nHolm-Bonferroni across the four family members, `α_family = 0.05`, two-sided. Verdict conditions per section (i).\n\n### v.4 Power and minimum detectable effect (D5 closed-form target)\n\n`D5` commits `|D_dis| ≥ 50`. Closed-form target.\n\n- **Discordant-pair framing (k = 2 path; sanity number for k = 5):** Let `n_disc = b + c` discordant pairs on the indicator `1{M_clean correct} ⊕ 1{M_raw correct}`. Under `H_1`, `b / (b + c) = π₁ ≠ 0.5`. Two-sided, `α = 0.05`, `n_disc = 50`: minimum detectable `π₁` at power 0.8 ≈ **0.69** (≈ 19 percentage-point skew) by normal approximation to the binomial test on `b`; equivalently the design detects any McNemar-style effect with odds ratio ≥ ~4 at `|D_dis| = 50`.\n- **Mean-difference framing (macro-F1 path, k = 5):** with `|D_dis| = 50` paired predictions, paired bootstrap `B = 2,000`, two-sided `α = 0.05`, target power 0.8, the smallest detectable standardised mean difference `|Δ_dis| / σ̂_Δ` ≈ 0.40. For anticipated `σ̂_Δ ≈ 0.15` on macro-F1 (typical for k = 5 noisy-label benchmarks), smallest detectable `|Δ_dis| ≈ 0.06` macro-F1 points. Threshold `δ_co = 0.05` is therefore marginally powered at exactly `|D_dis| = 50`; any drop below forces a power-correction rerun or downgraded INCONCLUSIVE verdict.\n- **|D_dis| ≥ 50 precondition** is enforced; if not achieved, mark `INCONCLUSIVE — INSUFFICIENT D_dis POWER` and rerun.\n- **Power table:** `|D_dis| ∈ {50, 75, 100, 150, 200}` × `δ_co ∈ {0.04, 0.05, 0.07, 0.10}`, entries computed by parametric bootstrap of conditional macro-F1 delta under OP-A noise at declared rates. Computed at runtime (pure Python); stated here only as a closed-form target.\n\n### v.5 FWER control\n\n- Holm-Bonferroni within each metric's family at `α_family = 0.05`, two-sided.\n- Primary metric family: macro-F1 (m = 4 sub-tests above).\n- Secondary metric families (accuracy, error rate) reported without FWER correction; failure on those does not invalidate the primary verdict but is recorded in the audit log.\n- Cross-metric comparison (positive accuracy overriding null macro-F1) is **not** permitted; primary metric is decisive.\n\nEOF\necho \"chunk4 OK\"; wc -c /workspace/final_design.md", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-fa9b4508-7c0c-4c05-860a-72f144e1bb4a", "tool_call": {"id": "call-fa9b4508-7c0c-4c05-860a-72f144e1bb4a", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Append section (v) as chunk 4\", \"command\": \"cat >> /workspace/final_design.md <<'EOF'\\n\\n---\\n\\n## (v) Pre-registered analysis plan\\n\\n### v.1 Metrics\\n\\n- **Primary:** macro-F1 (unweighted mean of per-class F1 over `k = 5` classes).\\n- **Secondary:** accuracy, error rate (`1 \\u2212 accuracy`).\\n- **Agreement / quality descriptors:** Cohen's \\u03ba between `y_gpt` and `y_human` on `D_gold \\\\ REQUIRES_REVIEW`; UNCERTAIN rate; adjudicator-vs-both disagreement rate; per-annotator inter-annotator agreement.\\n\\n### v.2 Statistical tests (D3, D4)\\n\\n- **Whole-evaluation gate (gate 1):**\\n  - Paired macro-F1 difference `\\u0394_full = macroF1(M_clean, D_test) \\u2212 macroF1(M_raw, D_test)` with paired bootstrap 95% CI, `B = 2,000` resamples.\\n  - Pre-registered effect-size threshold `\\u03b4_te = 0.05` for k = 5 (binary `\\u03b4_te = 0.03` if k = 2 in any branch).\\n  - Two-sided paired permutation test on per-item class-correctness indicators, `M = 10,000` permutations, with the same `m = 4` family Holm-Bonferroni structure (gate 1 = member 1, gate 2 primary = member 2, SL-1 replication = member 3, SL-3 null = member 4; SL-2 not in FWER family).\\n- **Conditional test (gate 2 primary):**\\n  - Computed on `D_dis_train_o