{"id": "b261eb1a-1451-4dd1-b9d0-be136f7fd5e9", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T13:44:36.596826", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "87450db2-0dac-45fb-a26f-74d97245f485", "action": {"command": "cat >> /workspace/final_design.md <<'EOF'\n\n---\n\n## (vi) Feasibility and budgeting under the actual runtime\n\n### vi.1 Hard environmental constraints (declared)\n\n- `network: disabled`; no pip-equivalent package installation; system Python 3.12.3 only; no GPU; 24 CPU cores; no Docta tool installed; no ChatGPT endpoint exposed.\n- These constraints are **hard** and not circumvented.\n\n### vi.2 What runs *offline* under these constraints\n\n| Component | Runtime/mode | Resource |\n|---|---|---|\n| Synthetic dataset generation (OP-A, `D_synth`, `D_train`, `D_gold`, `D_test`) | Offline, deterministic | seconds; 1 CPU |\n| Backbone training of `h` (logistic regression) | Offline | minutes; 1 CPU |\n| D-mock Docta transformation (iii.3 steps 1–3) | Offline, deterministic given seed | minutes; 1 CPU |\n| `M_raw` and `M_clean` training (`L2`-multinomial logistic regression) | Offline | minutes; 1–4 CPUs |\n| Paired bootstrap, paired permutation, Cohen's κ | Offline, pure Python | minutes; 1 CPU |\n| Noise-rate reruns (OP-B control SL-4) | Offline | hours; trivially parallelisable, 3 CPU cores × rep factor |\n| Pseudo `M_shuf` null | Offline | minutes; 1 CPU |\n\n**Total CPU-hours for offline components (estimate, not measured — runtime-fillable):** ≈ 3–10 CPU-hours for the headline run; ≈ 9–30 CPU-hours if SL-4 is requested. Well within the 24-CPU single-run budget.\n\n### vi.3 What is *mocked* with documented substitutions\n\n- **Docta** = D-mock iii.3 (committed; logged as `docta_mock_v1.confusion_matrix_aware.bounded_em.k5_lambda_freeze`).\n- **ChatGPT** = frozen prompt + frozen snapshot + (if endpoint unreachable) deterministic seeded surrogate from backbone `h(x; θ)` (iii.4). Surrogate substitution logged in every results table header.\n- **No third-party ML libraries** required; b