{"id": "4f98f4e8-a8cd-4aa0-a376-0074f71783a3", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T13:45:01.575060", "source": "environment", "parent_id": "1199f218-073b-4a42-9e51-f548b28278b4", "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-18f278ba-e539-4f28-ac8e-3ae5950f3dbc", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"phase\": \"exploration\", \"command\": \"echo \\\"--- iii.3 D-mock full ---\\\"; sed -n '77,108p' /workspace/final_design.md; echo \\\"--- v.3 decision table ---\\\"; sed -n '185,196p' /workspace/final_design.md; echo \\\"--- vi.4 human-hours table ---\\\"; sed -n '242,260p' /workspace/final_design.md\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.068, \"output\": \"--- iii.3 D-mock full ---\\n### iii.3 Docta D-mock transformation (committed; frozen now)\\n\\nA specific, seeded, probabilistic, confusion-matrix-aware label-denoising transformation. **Not** the abstract class.\\n\\n**Inputs (committed):**\\n- Training stream with raw labels `y_raw` on items in `D_train`.\\n- Declared noise matrix `Q_raw` (symmetric, OP-A injection at `p = 0.30`, k = 5): `Q[ty, ky] = P(noisy = ty | true = ky)`.\\n- Document-level seed `s`.\\n\\n**Algorithm (frozen):**\\n\\n1. **Backbone training (one-time):** fit an `L2`-regularised multinomial logistic regression `h` on `(x_i, y_raw[i])` for `i \\u2208 D_train`, with regularisation strength `\\u03bb` selected by 5-fold cross-validated held-out macro-F1 within `D_train`. Implementation: pure-Python fixed-step gradient descent, step `\\u03b7 = 1e-3`, `max_iter = 200`, `min_iter = 25`, convergence threshold `|L(\\u03b8_t) \\u2212 L(\\u03b8_{t\\u22121})| < 1e-5`. Per-class learning-rate scaling `\\u03b7_c = \\u03b7 / max(1, n_train_c / (N_train / k))`. Frozen seed `s` controls fold partitioning and stochastic tie-breaks. The resulting `h(x; \\u03b8)` is stored as a function and not retrained. (Runtime-fillable grid: `\\u03bb \\u2208 {1e-4, 1e-3, 1e-2, 1e-1}`, frozen once selected.)\\n2. **Iterative noise-matrix re-estimation (bounded EM):**\\n   - Initialise `Q_t \\u2190 Q_raw`.\\n   - For `t \\u2208 {1, 2, 3}`:\\n     - Compute posterior `P(true = ky | x_i, y_raw[i]) \\u221d Q_t[y_raw[i], ky] \\u00b7 h(x_i; \\u03b8)[ky]`, renormalised.\\n     - `Q_new[ty, ky] = ( \\u03a3_i 1{y_raw[i] = ty} \\u00b7 P(true = ky | x_i, y_raw[i]) + \\u03b5 ) / ( \\u03a3_i P(true = ky | x_i, y_raw[i]) + k\\u03b5 )`, `\\u03b5 = 1e-3`.\\n     - `Q_t \\u2190 0.5 \\u00b7 Q_new + 0.5 \\u00b7 Q_t`.\\n     - If `\\u2016Q_t \\u2212 Q_{t\\u22121}\\u2016_\\u221e < 1e-3` break.\\n   - Output final `Q*` and per-item posterior.\\n3. **Final posterior and cleaned labels:** On each `i \\u2208 D_train`, `P*(true = ky | x_i, y_raw[i]) \\u221d Q*[y_raw[i], ky] \\u00b7 h(x_i; \\u03b8)[ky]`, renormalised. Set `y_clean[i] = argmax_ky P*(true = ky | x_i, y_raw[i])`, deterministic tie-break: smallest class index.\\n4. **Output:** function mapping each `i \\u2208 D_train` to `y_clean[i]` plus per-item posterior table.\\n\\n**Properties guaranteed by this commitment:**\\n- **Seed-deterministic:** identical inputs + identical `s` \\u21d2 identical `y_clean`.\\n- **Confusion-matrix-aware:** cleaning explicitly conditions on per-class confusion structure.\\n- **Probabilistic at each step:** posterior is genuinely Bayesian (point estimate under frozen estimator).\\n- **Pure-Python implementable** for committed bounds `d \\u2264 100`, `k = 5`.\\n- **Bounded compute:** EM capped at 3 iterations; in practice converges in 2 under the OP-A noise model.\\n\\nLogged in run record as `docta_mock_v1.confusion_matrix_aware.bounded_em.k5_lambda_freeze`. The *only* D-mock used; no swap at runtime.\\n\\n--- v.3 decision table ---\\n### v.3 Decision rule (full, consolidated)\\n\\n| Gate | Test | Threshold | FWER family member |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Whole-eval paired permutation on `D_test`; CI excludes 0; `\\u0394_full \\u2265 \\u03b4_te` | `p_adj \\u2264 \\u03b1_family / 4` | 1 |\\n| 2 | Conditional paired permutation on `D_dis_train_of_test`; CI excludes 0; `\\u0394_dis \\u2265 \\u03b4_co` | `p_adj \\u2264 \\u03b1_family / 4`, `\\u03b4_co = 0.05` | 2 |\\n| 3 | SL-1 replication on `D_dis_repl`; CI excludes 0; same sign | `p_adj \\u2264 \\u03b1_family / 4` | 3 |\\n| 4 | SL-3 null \\u2014 `macroF1(M_shuf) \\u2264 1/k + 1e-2` | point estimate bound | 4 |\\n\\nHolm-Bonferroni across the four family members, `\\u03b1_family = 0.05`, two-sided. Verdict conditions per section (i).\\n\\n### v.4 Power and minimum detectable effect (D5 closed-form target)\\n--- vi.4 human-hours table ---\\n### vi.4 What is human-hours only\\n\\n| Task | Pool | Volume | Estimate |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Line annotation (D6, \\u2265 2 per `D_gold` item) | line annotators | `2 \\u00d7 |D_gold|` | baseline 1,800 labels at ~10 s/label \\u21d2 \\u2248 5 person-hours; conservative 30 s/label \\u21d2 ~15 person-hours |\\n| Line-annotator tie-break review | senior adjudicator (NEW role, Q3) | \\u2264 `|D_gold|`, tied to disagreement rate within `D_gold` | realistic 5\\u201315% disagreement rate \\u21d2 \\u2264 135 items \\u21d2 \\u2264 1 hour at 30 s/item |\\n| `D_dis` adjudication fold (Q3 invocation B) | senior adjudicator (NEW role, Q3) | `|D_dis|`, \\u2264 900 at maximum | at minimum `|D_dis| = 50` \\u21d2 ~25 min; at upper bound ~7.5 hours |\\n| Pipeline auditing (seed-frozen rerun, log inspection) | one engineer / senior | n/a | ~2 hours per run |\\n\\nThe senior adjudicator is committed to ~9 person-hours upper bound, ~25 minutes lower bound, **paid for separately and explicitly budgeted** as a line item distinct from line-annotator budget. This is the explicit Q3 NEW-role line.\\n\\nSurrogate ChatGPT or D-mock Docta do not consume human-hours.\\n\\n### vi.5 What is explicitly *not* in scope\\n\\n- Live runs of real ChatGPT or real Docta (network disabled; neither installed).\\n- OP-B noise-rate sweep executed only if a reviewer specifically requests it; headline verdict independent.\\n- Hum